__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.ruff_cache/
# Live e2e tier run records (tests/live): per-run evidence, never committed.
tests/live/runs/
build/
dist/
uv.lock

# Agent tooling (Claude Code skills, agent definitions) installed locally and
# not part of this project. The `otel-span-table` skill IS checked in, so it is
# re-included below; everything else under these paths is ignored.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/otel-span-table/
!.claude/skills/otel-span-table/**
skills-lock.json

# Per-developer Claude Code instructions. Claude Code reads `CLAUDE.local.md`
# alongside the tracked `CLAUDE.md`, so this is the seam for personal working
# preferences (verbosity, how to be corrected) that should not bind anyone else.
# Project-wide conventions — commit sign-off, the issue tracker, where domain
# docs live — belong in tracked `CLAUDE.md` instead, so every contributor and
# agent gets them from a clone.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Design-interrogation scratch (the `/grilling` skill's working notes). Local
# thinking-aloud, not a documented home for decisions: this repo is
# single-context, so settled reasoning belongs in `CONTEXT.md` (vocabulary) or
# `docs/adr/` (decisions) — see `docs/agents/domain.md`. Keeping a third
# location tracked would put design rationale in a place nothing references and
# no convention covers. Fold anything worth keeping into an ADR before the file
# goes stale; rejected alternatives and surfaced assumptions are the parts most
# often worth promoting.
.grill/

# Agent-workflow notes installed locally by the engineering skills (issue-tracker
# conventions, triage labels, how to consume the domain docs). Local tooling
# configuration rather than project documentation — the same reasoning as
# `.agents/` and `.claude/skills/` above.
#
# NOTE: tracked `CLAUDE.md` cites `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`,
# `triage-labels.md` and `domain.md`, so those three pointers dangle in a fresh
# clone. Deliberate: they tell an agent which conventions apply, and the files
# are reinstalled by the skill setup. If that trade stops being worth it, either
# inline the conventions into `CLAUDE.md` or track this directory — don't just
# drop the references.
docs/agents/

# Node/Playwright artifacts. The UI's own deps live under `ui/` (see the Vite
# section below); these are the root-level equivalents left behind when a
# browser install or an e2e run is driven from the repo root rather than `ui/`.
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# Pipeline runtime output
classification/output/

# React SPA build output (ADR-0019): the Containerfile's Node stage copies
# Vite's dist/ into data_governance/api/ui/ (the _UI_DIR the backend serves).
# The built assets are generated, never committed — keep only the .gitkeep.
/data_governance/api/ui/*
!/data_governance/api/ui/.gitkeep

# Local working notes for the two-span lineage branch — kept out of the PR
# deliberately; the wire contract (docs/sidecar-wire-contract.md) and
# ADR-0030 ship, these do not.
/docs/CUTOVER-two-span.md
/docs/REVIEWER-QUICKSTART.md
/docs/reading-the-sidecar-algorithm.md
